  "summary": "Second-stage dropper referencing litter.catbox.moe payload host",
  "details": "dist/src/example.js contains a reference to litter.catbox.moe, an anonymous, mutable file-hosting service used as a second-stage payload host in known npm supply-chain dropper campaigns. Fetching and executing content from this host on install or import lands attacker-controlled code in the installer's environment. The purpose of the package (metadata utility) does not require reaching an anonymous paste/file host, and litter.catbox.moe is not a legitimate distribution channel for package payloads.",
